Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi all,

I am working on a spatial model with a binomial outcome Y_i ~ Binomial(p_i, Ntrials=1). From a previous study, I have a vector of length i=1,...,n (n=271) of informative priors on each p_i. I see a built-in function for the prior of the form 'logitbeta' which I believe is what I want, but I would like to specify a unique param(a=, b=) for each observation based on my prior information. Is there a way to do this without listing each set of parameter sets individually? Perhaps specifying a param matrix?

Thanks,

Erica

f1 <- y ~ 1 + f(field, model=spde)

r1 <- inla(f1, family="binomial",
            data=inla.stack.data(stk.dat), verbose=TRUE,
            control.predictor=list(A=inla.stack.A(stk.dat),
                                   compute=TRUE))

results <- inla.spde2.result(r1, "field", spde, do.transf=TRUE)

