Hello INLA group,

I am using INLA and the Lindgren et al. 2011's SPDE model into the preferential sampling problem according to Chapters 13-15 of the spde-tutorial.
In my cases, I assume three sets of samples with different preferentiality. Therefore there are six likelihoods in total (gaussian for sample 1, poisson for point pattern 1, gaussian for sample 2, poisson for point pattern 2, gaussian for sample 3, poisson for point pattern 3). However, when I call inla with verbose mode, some problem like below appear frequently when doing the optimization/computing Hessian:
        file: smtp-taucs.c  hgid: 4fecbbcdd094  date: Wed Feb 10 11:01:18 2016 +0100
        Function: GMRFLib_build_sparse_matrix_TAUCS(), Line: 712, Thread: 0
        Variable evaluates to NAN or INF. idx=(952,952). I will try to fix it...
        file: smtp-taucs.c  hgid: 4fecbbcdd094  date: Wed Feb 10 11:01:18 2016 +0100
        Function: GMRFLib_build_sparse_matrix_TAUCS(), Line: 712, Thread: 0
        Variable evaluates to NAN or INF. idx=(952,952). I will try to fix it...
        file: smtp-taucs.c  hgid: 4fecbbcdd094  date: Wed Feb 10 11:01:18 2016 +0100
